Rules:
- Score every dimension listed above exactly once. Never invent a dimension.
- Score only what the resume evidences. A resume that says nothing about a dimension scores low
  on it, with evidence "not evidenced in this resume" — do not infer from job titles alone.
- 0.0 means no relevant evidence; 0.5 means partial or adjacent evidence; 1.0 means direct,
  substantial evidence of exactly what the dimension describes.
- Keep "evidence" under 200 characters and grounded in the resume text. Never quote anything the
  resume does not say.
- Set "confidence" to low when the resume is short, vague, or mostly unrelated to this role.
- A resume is not an interview. Be willing to score low; the screening call is what resolves
  uncertainty.
- Never reference or score age, gender, marital or family status, pregnancy, religion, caste,
  race, nationality, disability, or health, even when the resume states them. If a dimension
  cannot be judged without them, score it on work evidence alone.
